<title>FRANCE: Rolls-Royce wins engine order.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce wins engine order.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aero engine manufacturer Rolls-Royce Plc said on Monday it had won orders worth up to $200 million from Icelandair relating to four more Boeing 757 airliners and options on a further eight aircraft.</p>
<p>Rolls-Royce said at the Paris airshow the new aircraft, two 757-300s and two 757-200s will join Icelandair's existing fleet of four Rolls-Royce powered 757-200 planes.</p>
<p>The new 189-228 seat aircraft will be used on high density routes to North America, the company said.</p>
<p>The first two new 757-200 aircraft are due to be delivered in 1998-1999 with the 300 models following in 2001-2002.</p>
</text>
